{
  "_comment": [
    "AN-MANA-DRIVER-RULE-1 (2026-11-06). A target that can give MANA",
    "(every v6 and v7 size, Intel v5, Bsv2) needs a machine with a MANA driver.",
    "AMD v5 never gives MANA. One row per machine of the design.",
    "vm: the machine as the scan records it. size, os, agent (the release the",
    "Azure Linux Agent reports, name and version, or empty), image (publisher,",
    "offer, sku), primary (accelerated networking on the primary interface).",
    "expect: what the target advice gives (Get-VmfTargetAdvice) - offered (the",
    "supported options), refused (an option and its reason), start (both",
    "defaults), listing (linuxRelease.mana), manaUpgrade (linuxRelease.manaUpgrade).",
    "words: what the Details of the targets step say for that advice",
    "(src/dashboard/wizard.js, manaUpgradeText). An empty list: no such line.",
    "catalog: d (synthetic D sizes, Intel and AMD, v5 to v7) or b (the B v1 and",
    "Bsv2 catalog fixtures of centralus).",
    "Held by tests/unit/AnManaDriverRule.Tests.ps1 and tests/js/an-mana-driver-rule.test.js."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
